     "html": "Acne-prone skin is characterized by both non-inflammatory breakouts and inflammatory red, tender papules or cystic lesions. While this condition is more prevalent in individuals with oily skin, it can affect any skin type. Common triggers include incorrect product usage, hormones, diet, medication, genetics, and environmental factors. Appropriate management of acne requires addressing these factors in a comprehensive manner. To help target this skin concern, the following treatments and products might be right for you."
