       "text": "Hyperpigmentation/Sun Damage",
       "html": "Hyperpigmentation/Sun Damage"
      },
      {
       "t": "p",
       "html": "Hyperpigmentation is a common skin condition that occurs when certain patches of the skin appear visibly darker than the surrounding areas. These hyperpigmented areas are caused by an excess of melanin, a pigment-producing substance in human skin, eyes, and hair.<br><br> Common examples of hyperpigmentation include sun damage, acne marks, freckles, age spots, and melasma. Achieving an even skin tone can be challenging, but understanding hyperpigmentation is a crucial first step towards achieving clear, vibrant skin.<br><br> To help address this concern, we recommend the following list of treatments and products, which might be right for you."
      },
